{}{img_left}{photo.jpg}{photo}{160px}{}
I am a Ph.D. candidate in Econometrics and Statistics at the
[https://www.chicagobooth.edu/ University of Chicago Booth School of Business].
I received an M.S. in Statistics from the University of Chicago and a B.S. in Physics
from the Special Class for the Gifted Young at the University of Science and Technology of China.
~~~

== Research Interests
- *Time series*: covariance and precision matrix inference under long-range dependence, conformal prediction
- *Bayesian inference*: horseshoe priors, predictive inference
- *Graphical models*: high-dimensional Gaussian and functional graphical models
- *Simulation-based inference*: conditional flow matching, generative posterior samplers

